WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.617
LLM API performance has several layers.

00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:07.315
Prompt processing latency is the time spent reading the input context.

00:00:07.315 --> 00:00:11.073
Generation speed is often measured in tokens per second.

00:00:11.073 --> 00:00:17.045
Queueing delay appears when more requests arrive than the service can handle immediately.

00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:23.152
User experience depends on the combination of these factors, not a single benchmark number.

00:00:23.152 --> 00:00:31.340
Context windows affect serving performance because longer prompts consume more memory and increase prompt processing time.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.232
Concurrency increases pressure on CPU, GPU, RAM, and VRAM.

00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:40.668
Request size limits help prevent oversized prompts from overwhelming the service.

00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:47.714
Batch settings may improve throughput in some runtimes, but they can also increase latency or memory use.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:51.271
Performance tuning should be based on real workloads.

00:00:51.271 --> 00:01:01.337
Reliability practices include health checks, readiness checks, graceful failure, timeouts, cancellation, clear error responses, and fallback behavior.

00:01:01.337 --> 00:01:09.792
A health check should confirm that the service is available and able to respond as expected, not merely that a process exists.

00:01:09.792 --> 00:01:18.852
Fallback behavior might include a smaller model, a queued response, a retry policy, or a clear message that the service is unavailable.

00:01:18.852 --> 00:01:21.067
Scaling can be simple or complex.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:25.764
A small private API may need only one machine and conservative limits.

00:01:25.764 --> 00:01:33.347
A production service may need autoscaling, queue management, model warmup, load balancing, and capacity planning.

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:43.347
The engineering challenge is balancing throughput, cost, and user experience while preserving privacy, reliability, and clear operational boundaries.
